{
  "id": "dual-representation",
  "term": "dual representation",
  "definition": "Dual representation is the ability to understand that something can be both an object in its own right and a symbol for something else. In children’s learning, this means grasping that a picture or touch-screen image is itself a thing to interact with while also standing for something in the real world.",
